<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Copyright (C) 2026 longtimeno-c
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
  MediaViewer.app under the hardened runtime. Not sandboxed (the viewer opens
  any folder the user points it at); this lists only what the runtime would
  otherwise refuse.

  photos-library: Local search may index the system Photos library (issue #72,
  docs/design/17 "Photos library source"). Without it the hardened runtime denies
  PhotoKit silently. The permission prompt still belongs to the user, from a
  click in Settings; nothing reads the library until they allow it, and the
  base viewer never touches PhotoKit.

  automation.apple-events: Cmd+E on a Photos library item asks Photos to show
  it (its `spotlight` command; docs/design/26). The hardened runtime refuses
  every Apple Event without it. macOS still asks the user, once, before the
  first event reaches Photos; nothing else is sent to any app.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
